cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "DAPPREMO — Data Protection and Privacy Relationships Model"
message: >-
  If you use or refer to DAPPREMO, please cite the journal article indicated
  under "preferred-citation".
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Fabiano
    given-names: Nicola
    affiliation: "Studio Legale Fabiano, Rome, Italy"
abstract: >-
  DAPPREMO (Data Protection and Privacy Relationships Model) is a relational
  model for the personal data protection and privacy domains, based on set
  theory. Each area of activity is treated as a domain, that is, a set whose
  objects are its rules, activities and processes. The personal data protection
  domain is composed of legal rules together with non-homogeneous objects such
  as ethical principles, which belong to it by virtue of a shared characteristic
  property. The model describes the dynamic, multi-dimensional relations between
  such domains and between the individual objects they contain. This repository
  hosts the canonical, versioned specification of the model.
keywords:
  - DAPPREMO
  - data protection
  - privacy
  - GDPR
  - relational model
  - set theory
  - ethics
